1
00:00:01,756 --> 00:00:03,838
Chapter 75.

2
00:00:03,839 --> 00:00:08,558
The right whale's head. Contrasted view.

3
00:00:08,559 --> 00:00:15,755
Crossing the deck. Let us now have a good long look at the right whale's head.

4
00:00:15,756 --> 00:00:20,638
As in general shape, the noble sperm whale's head may be compared to a Roman

5
00:00:20,639 --> 00:00:26,719
war chariot, especially in front where it is so broadly rounded. So at a broad

6
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:31,198
view, the right whale's head bears a rather inelegant resemblance to a

7
00:00:31,199 --> 00:00:37,914
gigantic gallottoed shoe. 200 years ago an old Dutch voyager likened its shape

8
00:00:37,915 --> 00:00:44,079
to that of a shoemaker's last. And in this same last or shoe, that old woman

9
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:49,198
of the nursery tale with her swarming brood might very comfortably be lodged,

10
00:00:49,199 --> 00:00:51,999
she and all her progeny.

11
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,399
But as you come nearer to this great head, it begins to assume different

12
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:59,435
aspects according to your point of view.

13
00:00:59,436 --> 00:01:04,238
If you stand on its summit and look at these two F-shaped spout holes, you

14
00:01:04,239 --> 00:01:08,799
would take the whole head for an enormous base vial and these spiracles

15
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:11,594
the apertures in its sounding board.

16
00:01:11,595 --> 00:01:16,558
Then again, if you fix your eyes upon this strange crested comblike

17
00:01:16,559 --> 00:01:21,435
incrustation on the top of the mass, this green barnacled thing which the

18
00:01:21,436 --> 00:01:26,399
Greenlanders call the crown, and the southern fishers the bonnet of the right

19
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:31,518
whale, fixing your eyes solely on this, you would take the head for a trunk of

20
00:01:31,519 --> 00:01:37,198
some huge oak with a bird's nest in its crotch. At any rate, when you watch

21
00:01:37,199 --> 00:01:42,399
those live crabs that nestle here on this bonnet, such an idea will be almost

22
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:47,198
sure to occur to you, unless indeed your fancy has been fixed by the technical

23
00:01:47,199 --> 00:01:52,159
term crown also bestowed upon it, in which case you will take great interest

24
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:57,594
in thinking how this mighty monster is actually a diademmed king of the sea,

25
00:01:57,595 --> 00:02:02,799
whose green crown has been put together for him in this marvelous manner. But if

26
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:08,479
this whale be a king, he is a very sulky looking fellow to grace a diadem. Look

27
00:02:08,480 --> 00:02:14,238
at that hanging lower lip. What a huge sulk and pout is there. A sulk and pout

28
00:02:14,239 --> 00:02:20,479
by carpenters's measurement. About 20 ft long and 5 ft deep. A sulk and pout that

29
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:26,318
will yield you some 500 gallons of oil and more.

30
00:02:26,319 --> 00:02:31,838
A great pity now that this unfortunate whale should be hair lipped. The fisher

31
00:02:31,839 --> 00:02:37,198
is about a foot across. Probably the mother during an important interval was

32
00:02:37,199 --> 00:02:42,799
sailing down the Peruvian coast when earthquakes cause the beach to gape.

33
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:48,159
Over this lip, as over a slippery threshold, we now slide into the mouth.

34
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:53,359
Upon my word, were I at Meno, I should take this to be the inside of an Indian

35
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:59,594
wigwam. Good lord, is this the road that Jonah went? The roof is about 12 feet

36
00:02:59,595 --> 00:03:04,558
high and runs to a pretty sharp angle as if there were a regular ridge pole

37
00:03:04,559 --> 00:03:10,079
there. While these ribbed, arched, hairy sides present us with those wondrous

38
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:16,479
halfvertical scimitar-shaped slats of whale bone, say 300 on a side, which

39
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:21,198
depending from the upper part of the head or crown bone, form those Venetian

40
00:03:21,199 --> 00:03:25,679
blinds which have elsewhere been cursorally mentioned. The edges of these

41
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:29,999
bones are fringed with hairy fibers through which the right whale strains

42
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:35,435
the water, and in whose intricacies he retains the small fish, when openmouthed

43
00:03:35,436 --> 00:03:40,638
he goes through the seas of brit in feeding time. In the central blinds of

44
00:03:40,639 --> 00:03:45,594
bone, as they stand in their natural order, there are certain curious marks,

45
00:03:45,595 --> 00:03:50,638
curves, hollows, and ridges, whereby some whalemen calculate the creature's

46
00:03:50,639 --> 00:03:55,838
age, as the age of an oak by its circular rings. Though the certainty of

47
00:03:55,839 --> 00:04:01,198
this criterion is far from demonstrable, yet it has the savor of analogical

48
00:04:01,199 --> 00:04:06,719
probability. At any rate, if we yield to it, we must grant a far greater age to

49
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:11,198
the right whale than at first glance will seem reasonable.

50
00:04:11,199 --> 00:04:15,115
In old times, there seemed to have prevailed the most curious fancies

51
00:04:15,116 --> 00:04:20,479
concerning these blinds. One voyager in purchase calls them the wondrous

52
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:23,198
whiskers inside of the whale's mouth.

53
00:04:23,199 --> 00:04:29,274
Another hogs bristles. A third old gentleman in Hackloot uses the following

54
00:04:29,275 --> 00:04:35,594
elegant language. Quote, "There are about 250 fins growing on each side of

55
00:04:35,595 --> 00:04:43,039
his upper chop which arch over his tongue on each side of his mouth." End quote.

56
00:04:43,040 --> 00:04:48,399
Footnote. This reminds us that the right whale really has a sort of whisker, or

57
00:04:48,400 --> 00:04:53,359
rather a mustache, consisting of a few scattered white hairs on the upper part

58
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:56,159
of the outer end of the lower jaw.

59
00:04:56,160 --> 00:05:01,359
Sometimes these toughs impart a rather brigandish expression to his otherwise

60
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:05,755
solemn countenance. End of footnote.

61
00:05:05,756 --> 00:05:12,079
As everyone knows, these same hogs bristles, fins, whiskers, blinds, or

62
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:16,638
whatever you please, furnish to the ladies their busks, and other stiffening

63
00:05:16,639 --> 00:05:22,159
contrivances. But in this particular, the demand has long been on the decline.

64
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:27,039
It was in Queen Anne's time that the bone was in its glory, the farthingale

65
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:33,435
being then all the fashion. And as those ancient dams moved about gay, though in

66
00:05:33,436 --> 00:05:37,999
the jaws of the whale, as you may say, even so in a shower, with like

67
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:42,954
thoughtlessness, do we nowadays fly under the same jaws for protection, the

68
00:05:42,955 --> 00:05:46,954
umbrella being a tent spread over the same bone.

69
00:05:46,955 --> 00:05:51,518
But now, forget all about blinds and whiskers for a moment, and standing in

70
00:05:51,519 --> 00:05:56,719
the right whale's mouth, look around you, aresh, seeing all these colonades

71
00:05:56,720 --> 00:06:01,838
of bone so methodically ranged about, would you not think you were inside of

72
00:06:01,839 --> 00:06:07,679
the great Harlem organ, and gazing upon its thousand pipes? For a carpet to the

73
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:12,954
organ, we have a rug of the softest turkey, the tongue, which is glued, as

74
00:06:12,955 --> 00:06:18,479
it were, to the floor of the mouth. It is very fat and tender and apt to tear

75
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:23,755
in pieces in hoisting it on deck. This particular tongue now before us, at a

76
00:06:23,756 --> 00:06:28,399
passing glance, I should say it was a six barreler, that is, it will yield you

77
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:31,359
about that amount of oil.

78
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:35,999
He this you must have plainly seen the truth of what I started with, that the

79
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:41,594
sperm whale and the right whale have almost entirely different heads. To sum

80
00:06:41,595 --> 00:06:47,359
up then, in the right whales there is no great well of sperm, no ivory teeth at

81
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:53,435
all, no long slender mandible of a lower jaw like the sperm whales. Nor in the

82
00:06:53,436 --> 00:06:58,479
sperm whale are there any of those blinds of bone, no huge lower lip, and

83
00:06:58,480 --> 00:07:03,999
scarcely anything of a tongue. Again, the right whale has two external spout

84
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:07,755
holes. The sperm whale only one.

85
00:07:07,756 --> 00:07:12,479
Look your last now on these venerable hooded heads while they yet lie

86
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:17,359
together, for one will soon sink unrecorded in the sea, and the other

87
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:20,799
will not be very long in following.

88
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:25,679
Can you catch the expression of these sperm whales there? It is the same he

89
00:07:25,680 --> 00:07:31,115
died with, only some of the longer wrinkles in the forehead now seem faded

90
00:07:31,116 --> 00:07:37,518
away. I think his broad brow to be full of a prairieike placidity born of a

91
00:07:37,519 --> 00:07:40,479
speculative indifference as to death.

92
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:42,878
But mark the other head's expression.

93
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:48,399
See that amazing lower lip pressed by accident against the vessel's side so as

94
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:53,999
firmly to embrace the jaw. Does not this whole head seem to speak of an enormous

95
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:57,359
practical resolution in facing death?

96
00:07:57,360 --> 00:08:03,435
This right whale I take to have been a stoic? the sperm whale, a Plutonian who

97
00:08:03,436 --> 00:08:08,915
might have taken up Spinosa in his latter years.
